    90	| a>=2, c<2a | degree 4a is unique, with coefficient `-3A^4/16`; impossible, including c=0,1 |
    91	| a>=2, c>2a | degree 2c is unique, with coefficient `(2c-3)C^2`; impossible |
    92	| a>=2, c=2a | all three degree-4a terms must be added; they yield (UT) below and do cancel |
