   106	The denominator cannot vanish for an integer a>=2. Thus the full top equation is consistent at **every** a>=2. In particular, setting p=-1/4 would force a=3, but there is no license to set p=-1/4 for an arbitrary solution: the constant jet is a value at zero, not the leading ratio at infinity. At a>=4 neither leading root equals -1/4, which is consistent with a hypothetical non-proportional solution.
