   116	**4. Every coefficient-field factor and every polynomial-range pivot.**
   117	
   118	For each m>=2, `Q[d]/(3d^2-m)` is a quadratic field unless `m=3s^2` for an integer s>=1. In that case it is the product of the two rational fields d=s and d=-s, treated separately. In the irreducible case both embeddings into the algebraic closure are covered by an exact computation over the whole quadratic field. No convenient modular split root substitutes for either treatment.
