    72	For k=2 this is `-c t^-4`, NOT `-c`. Its pole cannot be ignored by
    73	describing the pair as Laurent. Inversion constantizes exponent k=-2,
    74	which is not the charged receiver. Therefore Theorem 2.6 cannot be
    75	applied to the inverted pair by the claimed constant-J hypothesis.
