   116	[P,Q]=-2 gamma^2.
   117	```
   118	
   119	At ordinary weight `(1,1)`, ell(P)=P, of positive weight 2.
   120	There is NO polynomial E with `[E,P]=P`. Indeed, term by term,
   121	
   122	```text
   123	[gamma^i pi^j, gamma*pi]=(i-j)gamma^i pi^j.             (DIAG)
   124	```
   125	
   126	The coefficient of `gamma*pi` in `[E,P]` is therefore always zero,
   127	while in P it is one. The same proof excludes E even in the original
   128	Laurent ring `K[gamma,gamma^-1,pi]`. In particular, no degree-2
   129	polynomial Euler element of the kind used for D108 exists. Importing
   130	GGV1's endpoint prohibition would also wrongly forbid this actual
   131	receiver's endpoint `(1,1)`.
