   322	### Full-spectrum ideation — at least every 12 hours
   323	
   324	No more than 12 hours may pass between completed full rounds. A significant
   325	event starts one sooner. Each round follows this protocol:
   326	
   327	1. **Freeze a state packet.** Record UTC time, clean basis commit, newer local
   328	   hashes if any, newest `LIVE STATE`, active/recent lane reports, review debt,
   329	   current `APPROACHES.md`, load-bearing `AUDIT.md` corrections, and all new
   330	   external evidence since the prior round.
   331	2. **Blind independent scan.** Every active research agent is a core ideator by
   332	   default and reads the whole avenue map, current gaps, and new evidence
   333	   before seeing the other submissions. A noninterruptible compute or review
   334	   worker may be omitted explicitly; mark the round degraded if this leaves
   335	   inadequate coverage. A rotating specialist lens may be added only after
   336	   the common scan. Model diversity is preferred; duplicate instances still
   337	   think independently.
   338	   After the September6 1210Z round, the automatic whole-portfolio roster is
   339	   Astra, Fable, and Sol. Opus and Grok are bounded utility seats and may be
   340	   invited for a concrete additional lens. Current1210Z invitations remain.
   341	   Whole-portfolio models are invited automatically. Each receives the
   342	   same sealed packet, submission contract, tool boundary, and deadline, and
   343	   must submit before seeing any other lane's report.  Every submission
   344	   receives equal post-deduplication consideration: model identity is neither
   345	   a bonus nor a vote, and operational unavailability degrades but does not
   346	   block the round.
   347	3. **Required submission contract.** Each report gives:
   348	   - a compact disposition vector over every numbered avenue: `unchanged`,
   349	     `raise`, `lower`, or `reopen`, with reasons for every change;
   350	   - a reranking of the principal proof and disproof bottlenecks;
   351	   - one genuinely new mechanism, or an explicit `NO_NEW_MECHANISM` with
   352	     evidence that the best use of capacity is an existing unresolved target;
   353	   - at least one new connection between existing avenues;
   354	   - the strongest proof attack and strongest counterexample/falsification
   355	     attack;
   356	   - one software acceleration or decisive experiment;
   357	   - a short campaign-systems check, independent of the mathematical software
   358	     proposal: either an `UPGRADE` card with the smallest useful test or
   359	     implementation, or `NO_CHANGE` with evidence.  Rotate across state
   360	     freshness, context and retrieval cost, claim/review propagation,
   361	     duplication, model routing and utilization, adapter reliability, AWS
   362	     scheduling and cost, reproducibility, and operator/chat-summary quality;
   363	   - no more than three detailed idea cards, each with explicit dependencies,
   364	     cheapest discriminator, interpretation of each outcome, stop condition,
   365	     and expected information gain;
   366	   - a `continue / redesign / stop` recommendation for current major lanes.
   367	4. **Deduplicate after collection.** Fingerprint ideas by target obstruction,
   368	   mechanism, object, and decisive test. Merge operational duplicates while
   369	   preserving independent origins, disagreements, and genuinely different proof
   370	   mechanisms. Shared wording is not independent support.
   371	5. **Cross-pollinate adversarially.** Only after blind collection, ask lanes to
   372	   combine compatible ideas, expose shared hidden assumptions, attack the
   373	   strongest proposal, and design the cheapest experiment that separates the
   374	   leading choices.
   375	6. **Run the canonical history/priority checksum.** Before compute, search
   376	   `AUDIT.md`, `APPROACHES.md`, `PROGRESS.md`, the newest `LIVE STATE`,
   377	   `ladder/REDUCTION.md`, and repository reports for every surviving target,
   378	   mechanism, and close synonym. Reconcile the master known-degree/closed-case
   379	   ledgers, then check each load-bearing literature claim in primary text.
   380	   Label every card `NEW`, `KNOWN`, `DUPLICATE`, or `SCOPE-CONFLICT` in the
   381	   synthesis. Blind consensus never overrides a banked exact result or primary
   382	   theorem; a shared stale packet premise is correlated error, not a vote.
   383	7. **Synthesize and launch.** The coordinator writes a ranked synthesis,
   384	   updates the avenue/claim graphs if needed, assigns owners and reviewers,
   385	   launches reversible lanes immediately, and records why alternatives were
   386	   deferred or stopped.  Deduplicate the systems checks, choose at most one
   387	   highest-value bounded upgrade for immediate work, and track it only in the
   388	   canonical `LIVE STATE` queue.  Trial at least one incremental machinery
   389	   improvement in every rolling 48-hour window unless no candidate clears its
   390	   measured benefit, regression-risk, and mathematical-opportunity-cost gate;
   391	   record a reasoned `NO_UPGRADE` rather than changing machinery for its own
   392	   sake.  Systems work runs beside, and normally does not block, live
   393	   mathematical research.
   394	
   395	Target 60 minutes for blind submissions, 30 for cross-pollination, and 30 for
   396	synthesis. Close a round within two hours when possible; if an ideator misses
   397	the close, mark the round `DEGRADED` instead of blocking ongoing research.
   398	Events arriving after the snapshot are queued for the next micro/full round
   399	and never silently mutate the sealed packet.
   400	
   401	Round artifacts use
   402	`xmodel/ideation-<YYYYMMDDTHHMMZ>-<lane>.md` and
