   551	## Replayability and operational safety
   552	
   553	- Computational claims ship engines, certificates, exact replay commands,
   554	  versions, input hashes, seeds, host, UTC times, and meaningful negative
   555	  controls. Mod-p work records every prime.
   556	- A claimed `python -O` or `-OO` verification is admissible only when every
   557	  load-bearing check remains live in that mode. Freeze an AST scan showing no
   558	  `Assert` nodes in the verification paths (or prove that any remaining
   559	  asserts are non-gating diagnostics), and run a deliberate old-pass/new-fail
   560	  mutation under every claimed interpreter mode. Byte-identical positive
   561	  output alone is insufficient: stripped checks can print the same answer
   562	  vacuously. Ordinary-only scripts may use `assert` only when the report labels
   563	  that limitation and makes no optimized-mode evidence claim.
   564	- A successor residual at digit `n` is typed only after an exact numerator `N`
   565	  is proved divisible by `p^n` on the charged predecessor scheme and
   566	  `N/p^n mod p` is derived with all lower-order divided carries retained. If
   567	  the quotient is not integral on that scheme, or generated coefficient rows
   568	  disagree with an exact determinant/source-identity reconstruction, the gate
   569	  is `TYPE-FAIL` and must not be used downstream.
   570	- msolve 0.10.1 characteristic-zero `-g` may return a first-machine-prime
   571	  unit basis before rational reconstruction while printing a characteristic-0
   572	  header. A char-0-header `[1]` is only first-prime trace evidence unless an
   573	  independently checked exact rational certificate is present. See `AUDIT.md`.
   574	- Run all heavy or uncertain-duration campaign computation on AWS, never on
   575	  the local machine. This includes CAS/solver jobs, Lean builds, and long or
   576	  potentially multi-GB exact-Python replays/enumerations. Reserve local
   577	  execution for editing, orchestration, hashing, status checks, model-review
   578	  adapters without compute tools, and genuinely short low-memory validation.
   579	  Follow `ops/FLEET.md` for machine inventory, shipping, caps, telemetry, and
   580	  kill safety.
   581	- `jc2-lean` is a separately owned nested repository and is outside the
   582	  campaign's inspection boundary. Campaign agents must not enter, enumerate,
   583	  search, read, build, status, modify, or control it. Scope every parent Git
   584	  query explicitly away from that path; never stage its gitlink. The parent
   585	  `.ignore` excludes it from ripgrep-style broad searches. Concurrent local
   586	  formalization may consume shared CPU/RAM, but campaign contention checks
   587	  remain system-level and must not identify or inspect that nested workload.
   588	- New heavy runners fail closed off AWS before importing a CAS or allocating
   589	  large objects, require a registered AWS job tag, and record the remote
   590	  hostname in custody.  New counterexample/frontier runners also record the
   591	  classical admissibility verdict described above before launch.  A
   592	  coordinator process-tree/swap-delta audit
   593	  is part of each live-state checkpoint; allocated swap without new pageouts
   594	  is historical occupancy, not by itself active thrashing.
   595	- A process-group guard is valid only if its recorded group includes the
   596	  actual CAS and every descendant whose RSS or lifetime it must control.
   597	  Wrappers that create an unrecorded inner PGID (including GNU `timeout`
   598	  without `--foreground`) are forbidden unless every inner group is itself
